3. Core enhanced notification rule
3.1 Configuration
String daysBefore = "30,15,7";
String trainingMode = "ALL";
String scanOnly = (String) config.get("scanOnly");
boolean isScanOnly = "true".equalsIgnoreCase(scanOnly);
The scanOnly setting is task-controlled. In the last shared source, the 30/15/7 intervals and ALL mode are still hardcoded; do not describe them as fully task-driven. The rule validates scanOnly and uses a separate allowEmailSending safety flag.
3.2 Dynamic course discovery
SELECT DISTINCT COURSE_ID FROM TRAINING
WHERE COURSE_ID IS NOT NULL AND EXPIRES IS NOT NULL
AND DATEDIFF(DAY, CAST(GETDATE() AS DATE), CAST(EXPIRES AS DATE)) IN (?,?,?)
ORDER BY COURSE_ID
The rule obtains a JDBC connection via context.getJdbcConnection(), binds the notification intervals, and discovers distinct courses with training records in the relevant date windows. DISTINCT avoids processing the same course repeatedly simply because many users hold it.
3.3 Training record retrieval and identity resolution
getUsersToNotify(courseId, expirationDate, context);
The existing SAP Training Table Rule Library queries TRAINING for CORPID where COURSE_ID and EXPIRES match. Each returned corporate ID is resolved to a SailPoint Identity; missing identities are tracked.
3.4 Policy evaluation and new eligibility gate
getAccessLostIfTrainingExpires(nextIdentity, thisCourseId);
The SAP Training Policy Rule Library iterates IdentityEntitlement records, resolves ManagedAttribute or Bundle metadata using getManagedAttributeOrBundle(), and derives training requirements through getRequiredTrainingFromEntity(). Existing NERC/HIPAA flags can identify training-dependent access independently of the explicit revoke checkbox.
boolean revokeEnabled = Util.otob(attrs.get("revokeOnExpTraining"));
String requiredCourse = (String) attrs.get("requiredCourse");
if (!revokeEnabled || Util.isNullOrEmpty(requiredCourse)) continue;
List requiredCourses = Util.csvToList(requiredCourse);
if (requiredCourses.contains(thisCourseId)) qualifyingEntitlements.add(identityEnt);
This additional filter enforces the JIRA-specific conditions. The list of potentially impacted access is replaced by the qualifying list. If no qualifying entitlement remains, the identity/course notification is skipped.
