Inventory: 23,071 training records, 5 courses, 13,869 distinct CORPIDs. The 9999-12-31 expiration value appears for some courses and should be clarified as a possible sentinel. This is a read-only inventory rule, not a runtime notification dependency.
5.2 TEST-Rule-TrainingExpiration
Queries selected CORPIDs for course IDs, EXPIRES, and DATEDIFF days left, initially restricting to exact 7/15/30-day windows. It confirmed candidate identities and highlighted that results change day to day as expiration dates move outside exact-day intervals. Later debugging removed the date filter to inspect remaining days directly.
5.3 Test-Rule-TrainingEntitlementMapping
Retrieves IdentityEntitlement records for each selected identity using QueryOptions with identity.id, then resolves catalog ManagedAttribute records by application, attribute and value. It reports requiredCourse and revokeOnExpTraining without filtering on the checkbox. In this IIQ environment, IdentityEntitlement.getApplication() worked whereas getApplicationName() did not.
